1. What this licence covers
---------------------------
This licence covers the GalaxyOS Original Work: everything in GalaxyOS 2
that was written or made for GalaxyOS and is not a third-party component.
That includes the galaxy-* commands and the other GalaxyOS scripts in
/usr/local/bin and /usr/local/lib, the boot, init and configuration files
written for GalaxyOS (such as /etc/init.d/rcS and /etc/galaxy), the menus,
desktop configuration, themes, wallpaper, logo, icons and artwork, the
installer, updater and activation system, and the layout and arrangement
of the system as a whole.

It does NOT cover the free and open source components listed in NOTICE
(the Linux kernel, BusyBox, Firefox, LibreOffice and the others). Each of
those keeps its own licence, and nothing here limits your rights under
those licences. Their source code is available as described in NOTICE.

2. What you may do
------------------
If you have a valid copy of GalaxyOS 2 you may install it and use it on
your own computers or virtual machines, and make backup copies for
yourself.

3. What you may not do
----------------------
Unless bes gives you permission in writing, you may not:

  a) copy, republish, sell, rent, share or redistribute the GalaxyOS
     Original Work, alone or as part of another product;
  b) modify it, translate it, or make derivative works or "clones" based
     on it, including systems that copy its commands, menus, scripts,
     look, structure or file layout;
  c) reverse engineer, unpack, decompile or extract it in order to copy
     or reproduce it, except where the law allows this anyway;
  d) remove or change the copyright, trademark or licence notices;
  e) use any part of the GalaxyOS Original Work, its file structure or
     its documentation to train, fine-tune, evaluate or prompt any
     artificial intelligence or machine learning system, or put it into a
     dataset, code index or retrieval system for such systems;
  f) use automated tools, bots, scrapers or AI agents to collect, analyse
     or reproduce the GalaxyOS Original Work for any of the purposes in
     (a) to (e).

